# Sony PDX245 Telephony SELinux Policy (system_ext)
#
# Allow platform_app domain (qcrilmsgtunnel, ims) access to telephony HAL
# services. Stock Sony firmware grants these permissions in system_ext sepolicy,
# but GSI replaces system_ext and loses them.
#
# NOTE: This MUST be in SYSTEM_EXT_PRIVATE_SEPOLICY_DIRS, not BOARD_SEPOLICY_DIRS.
# BOARD_SEPOLICY_DIRS compiles as vendor policy which is on the vendor partition
# (not modified by GSI). Only SYSTEM_EXT policies are compiled into the system image.
#
# Without this policy:
# - qcrilmsgtunnel can't bind to IQtiOemHook AIDL service
# - OEM hook code 1028 goes unhandled -> RADIO_UNAVAILABLE
#
# Observed AVC denials:
#   avc: denied { find } for name=vendor.qti.hardware.radio.qcrilhook.IQtiOemHook/oemhook0
#     scontext=u:r:platform_app  tcontext=u:object_r:vendor_hal_telephony_service2
#     tclass=service_manager
#
#   avc: denied { find } for ... tcontext=u:object_r:hal_telephony_hwservice
#     tclass=hwservice_manager
#
# APPROACH: We cannot directly reference vendor_hal_telephony_service2 from
# system_ext policy (Treble policy split prevents it). Instead, we add
# platform_app to the hal_telephony_client attribute, which the VENDOR policy
# already grants access to vendor_hal_telephony_service2 through:
#   (allow hal_telephony_client vendor_hal_telephony_service2 (service_manager (find)))
# This is the Treble-correct way to bridge the system/vendor policy boundary.

# Add platform_app to hal_telephony_client attribute.
# Vendor policy already allows hal_telephony_client to find
# vendor_hal_telephony_service2 on service_manager and make binder calls
# to hal_telephony_server. On stock, ims/qcrilmsgtunnel run as
# vendor_qtelephony (which is in this attribute); on GSI they run as
# platform_app, so we need this bridge.
typeattribute platform_app hal_telephony_client;

# Also allow the legacy HIDL hwservice_manager path
allow platform_app hal_telephony_hwservice:hwservice_manager { find };
